  "question": {
    "text": "If the common tangents to the parabola, <math><msup><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>y</mi></math> and the circle, <math><msup><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math> intersect at the point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math>, then the distance of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math> from the origin (units), is:",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "P4nsd",
      "text": "<math><mn>2</mn><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfenced></math>",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "Yd34n",
      "text": "<math><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></math>",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PQoo2",
      "text": "<math><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></math>",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "V6egj",
      "text": "<math><mn>2</mn><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Let&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi></math>&nbsp;be the common tangent.</p><p>Then&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></math>&nbsp;(condition of tangency for circle)</p><p>Solving with&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>y</mi></math>, we get&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mfenced><mrow><mi>m</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>i.e.&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>m</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></math></p><p>Being a tangent,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></math>&nbsp;must have equal roots.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>m</mi></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>c</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo></math></p><p>From&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#38;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>c</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#38;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>c</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></math>&nbsp;(As&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>c</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><mn>0</mn></math>, so&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>c</mi><mo>&#8800;</mo><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></math>).</p><p>So, both tangents have common&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi></math>&nbsp;intercept and thus intersect at&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfenced></math>.</p><p>Thus, distance of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math>&nbsp;from origin is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mfenced><mrow><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;units.</p>",
    "image": null
  },
